  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Kaleesuwari Refinery Private Limited vs Intelligence Inspector on 29 August, 2013 Author: V.Chitambaresh Bench: V.Chitambaresh In The High Court Of Kerala At Ernakulam Present: The Honourable Mr.Justice V.Chitambaresh Thursday, The 5Th Day Of September 2013/14Th Bhadra, 1935 WP(C).No. 22125 of 2013 (M)",
    "facts": "EXHIBIT P3: COPY OF THE RELEVANT EXTRACT OF SCHEDULE I OF KVAT ACT 2003 DATED NIL. EXHIBIT P4: COPY OF THE DETENTION NOTICE ISSUED BY THE IST RESPONDENT UNDER SECTION 47(2) OF THE KERALA VALUE ADDED TAX ACT DATED 30/8/2013. EXHIBIT P5: COPY OF THE CERTIFICATE OF EXAMINATION ISSUED BY THE FOOD ANALYST TO GOVERNMENT, GOVERNMENT ANALYST'S LABORATORY, KAKKANAD DATED 24/8/2013. The petitioner seeks release of the goods detained under Ext.P4 notice. Ext.P4 notice inter-alia states as follows:- 'As per the documents accompanied, the goods under transport is refined coconut oil - a non taxable item. On physical verification, it is realised that the goods under transport is loosely consistent, odourless and colourless. The goods actually transporting is suspected to be inedible oil used for other industrial purposes taxable at 5%'. 2. The plea of stock transfer put-forth by the petitioner can be accepted only if the goods is established to be a coconut oil. Whether the goods is a refined coconut oil as claimed can be deciphered only in the adjudication proceedings. The Government Pleader points out that similar consignments have been released on Kaleesuwari Refinery Private Limited vs Intelligence Inspector on 29 August, 2013 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/196287859/ 3 orders of Court only after directing a portion of the security amount to be deposited. 3.",
